CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assignment from a lambda: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ implicit copy assignment: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ assignment operator template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ implicit move assignment: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
An assignment to a POD class took the built-in path and ignored the
class's assignment operator template (`g = [] {...}': "invalid implicit
conversion").  Once a specialization of the template had been
instantiated the class was no longer taken for POD, and as it has no
synthesized copy or move assignment, `c = static_cast<pod &&>(b)' found
no operator=.
